<!-- This is a sample slide deck to get started with.  If you want the slides to be built, -->
<!-- you must go to `project.ptx` and uncomment the slides targets (starting on line 12)   -->

<pretext xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <!-- Include the docinfo common to the course, in the parent folder (..) -->
  <xi:include href="../docinfo.ptx"/>

  <slideshow xml:id="slides">
    <title>Real Analysis Slides</title>

    <frontmatter>
      <titlepage-items/>
    </frontmatter>

    <!-- This assumes you want to structure your entire slide deck by sections -->
    <!-- RevealJS will use 2-d navigation: move left-right to switch between sections, up-down to switch between slides in a section -->
    <section xml:id="sec-1-1">
      <title>Constructing Number Systems</title>

      <slide>
        <title>Overview</title>
        <p pause="yes"> We explore a process for constructing number systems. </p>
        <p><ul pause="yes">
          <li>Use known number systems to construct new number systems.</li>
          <li>Outline a process of constructing number systems.</li>
          <li>Use process to construct the integers from the natural numbers.</li>
        </ul></p>
      </slide>

      <slide>
        <title>Real Numbers</title>
        <p pause="yes">We will be constructing real numbers from the rational numbers.</p>
        <p pause="yes">Assume rational numbers exist <m>\Rightarrow</m> Use to make real numbers.</p>
        <p pause="yes">Constructing number systems:</p>
        <p><ul pause="yes">
          <li>Develop an intuitive understanding of what the numbers are like.</li>
          <li>Make a list of axioms that precisely describes your number system.</li>
          <li>Construct a set and define any operations, relations, etc that are needed to create the number system and satisfy the axioms.</li>
          <li>Show that every construction is <q>equivalent</q> to your construction.</li>
        </ul></p>
      </slide>
    </section>

    <section xml:id="sec-1-2">
      <title>Section 1.2</title>
      <slide>
        <title>[topic]</title>
        <p>

        </p>
      </slide>
    </section>


  </slideshow>
</pretext>
